/-!
# Properties of modules on a scheme, read on its small étale site

Properties of Spaces, Section 05VR, consequences (4) and (5): if `X` is a scheme and `𝓕` is a
quasi-coherent module on `X_étale`, then for every property `𝒫` of that section other than
"coherent" and "locally free", `𝒫` holds for `𝓕` on `X_étale` exactly when it holds for `𝓕`
viewed as a quasi-coherent sheaf on the scheme `X`; and if `X` is locally Noetherian the same is
true for "coherent".  Both are Descent, Lemma 05VG, read through the equivalence `𝓕 ↦ 𝓕^a` of
Descent, Proposition 03DX between quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-modules and quasi-coherent modules on
`X_étale`.  For a scheme `X`, the site `X_étale` of the section is the small étale site of `X`.

The library states Descent, Lemma 05VG property by property in
`StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Descent.AssociatedModule.PropertiesOfModulesComparison`: for a
quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module `𝓕`, `𝓕` has `𝒫` exactly when `𝓕^a` has `𝒫`, at once on the big
sites, on `X_Zar` and on `X_étale` (`AlgebraicGeometry.SmallEtale.associatedModule`).  This file
registers those statements, and for the property "quasi-coherent" the fact that `𝓕^a` is
quasi-coherent on `X_étale`, as consequences (4) and (5) of Section 05VR.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 05VR](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05VR)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 05VG](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05VG)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DX](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DX)
-/

